consent-signed-in = Signed in as { $name }.
consent-signed-in-plain = You are signed in.
consent-intro = { $client } asks for the access below. Untick any access to your data you do not want to give, then choose Allow.
consent-scopes = Access to your data asked for
consent-fixed = Always part of signing in to { $client }
consent-choose = The access to your data you give
consent-logo = Logo of { $client }
consent-about-home = About { $client }
consent-about-policy = Privacy policy of { $client }
consent-about-terms = Terms of service of { $client }
consent-registered-itself = { $client } registered itself with this server. Its name, logo and links are its own, and no administrator has checked them.
scope-extension = Access this server defines for its own use: { $scopes }
consent-no-fhir-user = { $client } asks who you are as a FHIR resource, and your account is linked to no single record here, so it is not told. Ask the administrator of your account to link it.
consent-allow = Allow
consent-deny = Deny
fault-page = Something went wrong
fault-unknown-client = This app is not registered here
fault-unknown-client-body = The app asked for access with a client or a return address this server does not know. Go back to the app and try again, or ask its supplier.
fault-lapsed = This request has ended
fault-lapsed-body = The sign-in took too long or was already finished. Go back to the app and start again.
fault-other-browser = This sign-in began elsewhere
fault-other-browser-body = The sign-in did not begin in this browser, so it cannot finish here. Go back to the app and start again.
fault-bad-request = This request cannot be read
fault-bad-request-body = The address or the form was incomplete. Go back to the app and start again.
fault-own-record = Your own record cannot be opened here
fault-own-record-body = Your account names your own record, but this server does not let you read it, or holds no health record for it. Ask the administrator of this server, then open the app again.
fault-assurance = Your login is not strong enough here
fault-assurance-body = This server needs a login with a stronger means of electronic identification than the one you used. Log in again with a means at the level the server asks for.
fault-refused = This app's request cannot be accepted
fault-refused-body = The app registered itself with this server and asked for something it does not allow, so you are not sent back to it. Go back to the app and try again, or ask its supplier.
fault-server = The server could not complete this
fault-server-body = Something failed on our side. Try again in a moment.
no-scope-title = { $client } cannot be given any access for your account
no-scope-body-role = Your account holds no role that grants what { $client } asks for. A role that would: { $roles }. Ask the administrator of your account for it, then open { $client } again.
no-scope-body-client = { $client } asks for access this server does not give it. Ask the supplier of { $client } or the administrator of this server.
no-scope-back = Return to { $client }
consent-remember = Remember this choice for { $client }
consent-remember-help = Next time { $client } asks for the same access, you are not asked again. You can withdraw it on the page that lists your choices.
manage-page = Your choices
manage-title = Apps you allowed
manage-intro = These apps can reach your data: the ones you chose to remember, and the ones connected now. Disconnect an app and its access ends at once.
manage-none = No app keeps access to your data.
manage-offline = This app stays connected after you sign out, until you disconnect it.
manage-online = This app stays connected while you are signed in.
manage-organisation = Your organisation registered this app for its staff. Disconnect ends its access now; the app works again the next time you sign in to it.
manage-first-party = This is your organisation's own app. Disconnect ends its access now; the app works again the next time you sign in to it.
manage-disconnect = Disconnect
manage-scope = Access given
